cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Galois group of x(x-1)...(x-p+1)+1"
abstract: >-
  A Frobenius certificate for the symmetric group in odd prime degree: a monic
  irreducible whose Frobenius at an odd unramified prime q is both odd
  (Stickelberger) and fixed-point-free has Galois group S_p. For
  f_p = x(x-1)...(x-p+1)+1 the fixed-point-free condition is automatic at every
  q <= p, so the question reduces to a single Kronecker symbol
  (disc f_p / q) = -1 with q < p. That symbol is periodic in p, giving a
  computer-free proof that Gal(f_p/Q) = S_p for all primes p congruent to
  7, 13, 17, 19, 23, 29 mod 36 (Dirichlet density 1/2), raised to density 31/40
  using q = 5, together with verification for every odd prime p < 100000.
